G3049.d:
λογίζομαι
 (λόγος), [in LXX chiefly for חָשַׁב ;] 
  1. prop., of numerical calculation, to count, reckon: with accusative before μετά, Mark.15:23 (LXX) (Rec., R, mg.), Luke.22:37. 
  2. Metaphorical, without reference to numbers, by a reckoning of characteristics or reasons; 
  (a) to reckon, take into account: with accusative of thing(s), 1 Cor.13:5; id. before dative of person(s), Rom.4:3 (LXX), Rom.4:4, 6 4:8" (LXX), 2 Cor.5:19, 2 Tim.4:16; before εἰς (cf. Heb. ל חָשַׁב; Bl., § 33, 3), Acts.19:27, Rom.2:26 4:3, 5 4:9-11, 22-24 9:8 Gal.3:6" (LXX), Jas.2:23 (LXX); 
  (b) to consider, calculate: with accusative of thing(s), Phil.4:8; before ὅτι, John.11:50, Heb.11:10; τοῦτο, ὅτι, 2 Cor.10:11; with accusative of person(s), with inf., Rom.6:11; before ὡς, Rom.8:36 (LXX); 
  (with) to suppose, judge, deem: 1 Cor.13:11; ὡς, 1 Pet.5:12; οὕτως, 1 Cor.4:1; with accusative of thing(s), 2 Cor.3:5; id. before εἰς, 2 Cor.12:6; ὅτι, Rom.8:18; τοῦτο, ὅτι, Rom.2:3, 2 Cor.10:7; with inf., 2 Cor.11:5; accusative and inf., Rom.3:28 14:14, Phil.3:13; with accusative of person(s) before ὡς, 2 Cor.10:2; 
  (d) to purpose, decide: with inf. (Eur., Or., 555), 2 Cor.10:2 
 (cf. ἀνα-, δια-, παρα-, συλ-λογίζομαι).†
 (AS)

G3120.d:
μαλακός, -ή, -όν 
 [in LXX: Pro.25:15 (רַךְ) Pro.26:22 (לָהַם)* ;] 
soft; 
  1. prop., to the touch (opposite to σκληρός): of clothing, pl., Matt.11:8, Luke.7:25. 
  2. Of persons and their mode of living; 
  (a) mild, gentle; 
  (b) soft, effeminate: 1 Cor.6:9 (prob. in obscene sense, cf. Deiss., LAE, 150, 4; MM, xvi; Zorell, see word).†
 (AS)

G3128.d:
Μανασσῆς, -ῆ, ὁ (Heb. מְנַשֶּׁה), 
 Manasseh; 
  1. (a) the first-born son of Joseph; 
  (b) the tribe which bore his name: Rev.7:6. 
  2. King of Judah: Matt.1:10.†
 (AS)

G3173.d:
μέγας, μεγάλη, μέγα, 
 [in LXX chiefly for גָּדוֹל, also for מַרְבֶּה ,רַב (incl. μείζων), רֹב (μέγιστος) ;] 
great; 
  1. of external form, bodily size, measure, extent: λίθος, Matt.2:60; δράκων, Rev.12:3; ἰχθῦς, John.21:11; πόλις, Rev.11:8; μάχαιρα, Rev.6:4, al. 
  2. Of intensity and degree: δύναμις, Acts.4:33; φόβος, Mark.4:41; ἀγάπη, John.15:13; ἄνεμος, 'ib. 6:18; κραυγή, Acts.23:9; φῶς, Matt.4:16; πυρετός, Luke.4:38; θλίψις, Matt.24:21. 
  3. Of rank; 
  (a) of persons: θεός (MM, xvi), Titus.2:13; Ἄρτεμις, Acts.19:27; compar. (see infr.), Matt.18:1 (cf. Dalman, Words, 113f.); neut. for masc. (Bl., §32, 1), Matt.12:6; 
  (b) of things: ἁμαρτία, John.19:11; μυστήριον, Eph.5:32; = μεγίστη (see infr., and cf. Field, Notes, 16f.), Matt.22:36; compar. for superl. (M, Pr., 78), 1 Cor.13:13. 
  4. 
  (a) Compar., μείζων: Matt.11:11 23:17, al.; neut. pl., μείζονα, contr. μείζω, John.1:51; double compar., μειζότερος (M, Pr., 236; Bl., §11, 4), III Jo 4; 
  (b) superl, μέγιστος (Deiss., BS, 365), 2 Pet.1:4.
 (AS)

